module gunbc.plans.v2_complexity_capability_parity

import gunbc.plan { Plan, DissolutionTrigger, HasTrigger }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock, MarkdownTableRow, TableBlock, BlockquoteBlock, CodeBlock, AlignNone }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { h2, h3, p, li, ul, ol, cell, row }

fn v2_complexity_capability_parity_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    BlockquoteBlock { blocks: [
      p(text: "**Status: DRAFT for operator review (2026-08-04).** Design-note-first: **no code lands from this note.** It answers one question — *is v2 complexity analysis anemic compared to v1?* — with a verdict grounded in the tree's own status carriers, and declares the migration program that closes the gap."),
      p(text: "**Verdict: yes, and the tree already says so in its own enforcement model.** The anemia is real, it is localized (see §2 — it is *not* the whole cost stack), and one carrier currently declares it **permanent**, which is the finding worth acting on first (§4)."),
    ] },

    h2(text: "1. Scope seam with the sibling note (DESIGN §3 — do not fork)"),
    p(text: "This note and [`discrete-cost-derivation.md`](discrete-cost-derivation.md) are two halves of one program and must not restate each other. The split is by *question*:"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [
        cell(text: "Question"),
        cell(text: "Owner"),
      ]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "What can the engine *express and derive*? (cost algebra, work/span, output size, peak space, interprocedural summaries, recursion)"),
          cell(text: "**this note**"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "What does a derivation *mean and get used for*? (subject binding, valuation at a declared input, honesty states, cost justification, witness admission)"),
          cell(text: "[`discrete-cost-derivation.md`](discrete-cost-derivation.md)"),
        ]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "**Consequence, stated so neither note quietly grows into the other:** the expression-algebra promotion and the work/span/space summary — which the sibling note originally listed under its C0 and C2 — are **this note's C1 and C2** and have been removed from that note's scope. The valuation environment and the admission consumer remain **its** C1 and C5 and are absent here. **The authority ruling has exactly one home: §5 of this note**, signed as C0 deliverable (a) in §7. The sibling note's C0 is now purely a dependency edge on that signature — it states no ruling of its own, so there is no second place for the two to drift apart."),

    h2(text: "2. The verdict, and its exact boundary"),
    p(text: "**The cost half is live; the complexity half is not.** This distinction matters, because over-scoping the fix would be a second error. From `v2.lens.enforcement.contract`:"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [
        cell(text: "Contract"),
        cell(text: "Mode"),
        cell(text: "Consumer witness"),
        cell(text: "Boundary class"),
      ]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`lens_contract_cost`"),
          cell(text: "**`Blocking`**"),
          cell(text: "**`BoundConsumerWitness`** (`complexity_gate/budget_roster_completeness_test.dag`)"),
          cell(text: "`WallNow`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`lens_contract_complexity`"),
          cell(text: "`AuditOnly`"),
          cell(text: "**`NoConsumerWitness`**"),
          cell(text: "**`RatchetForever`**"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`lens_contract_complexity_accumulator_copy`"),
          cell(text: "`AuditOnly`"),
          cell(text: "`NoConsumerWitness`"),
          cell(text: "`WallAfterGrounding`"),
        ]),
        row(cells: [
          cell(text: "`lens_contract_complexity_linearity_audit`"),
          cell(text: "`AuditOnly`"),
          cell(text: "`NoConsumerWitness`"),
          cell(text: "—"),
        ]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "So the generic structural engine `v2.lens.cost` is a real, enrolled, blocking wall — it is not a stub, and this program does not touch its kernel. Everything *above* it is audit-only with no consumer: the projection lens and all three specialized complexity lenses. That is the DESIGN §6 **coverage-by-illusion tier**, stated by the repo about itself."),
    p(text: "A second, sharper tell sits inside the projection lens: `v2.lens.complexity` `complexity_variables_admits` is"),
    CodeBlock { code: "fn complexity_variables_admits(xs: List<SizeVariable>) -> Bool \{\n  true\n\}\n" },
    p(text: "— a `Validation` whose admission predicate is the constant `true`. It refines nothing; the `Refined<List<SizeVariable>>` carrier it feeds is a type name standing where a constraint was supposed to be. DESIGN §4b names this class exactly: *'richer type names are not safety — a brand, wrapper, or `Validated<T>` is cosmetic until construction and acceptance enforce the distinction.'*"),

    h2(text: "3. Capability comparison (verified, not recalled)"),
    p(text: "`src/v1/complexity.dag` is 4,857 lines and 171 declarations. What it carries that v2 does not:"),
    TableBlock {
      header: row(cells: [
        cell(text: "Capability"),
        cell(text: "v1"),
        cell(text: "v2"),
      ]),
      alignments: [AlignNone, AlignNone, AlignNone],
      rows: [
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Asymptotic class + dominance lattice"), cell(text: "yes"), cell(text: "**yes** (and better factored)")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Symbolic cost expression"), cell(text: "`CostConst/Add/Mul/Max/Sum/Log/Extern/Unknown`"), cell(text: "partial — no `Max`, no binder-carrying `Sum`, no extern")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Size expression"), cell(text: "`SizeConst/SizeVar/SizeLen/SizeAdd/SizeMax`"), cell(text: "**none** — `SizeVariable { source: Node }` only")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Exact summation over a bounded collection"), cell(text: "`CostSum { binder, upper, body }`"), cell(text: "**no**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Work vs span"), cell(text: "both, on `ComplexitySummary`"), cell(text: "**neither**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Output-size derivation"), cell(text: "`output_size: Map<String, CostExpr>`"), cell(text: "**no**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Peak space"), cell(text: "`peak_space: CostExpr?`"), cell(text: "**no**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Certainty"), cell(text: "`Proven | Conservative`"), cell(text: "**no**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Interprocedural function summaries"), cell(text: "`CostInternTable` memo"), cell(text: "**no**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Call graph / SCC"), cell(text: "by import from `std.graph`"), cell(text: "**not consumed** — corrected by census, see C0(b) finding 1")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Recursion / descent bounds"), cell(text: "vocabulary shared (`std.termination` / `std.computation` / `std.induction`); **walkers** v1-AST-local"), cell(text: "loop-bound edge only")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Parser-progress reasoning"), cell(text: "yes (mutual recursion)"), cell(text: "**no**")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Concrete-input evaluation"), cell(text: "partial machinery"), cell(text: "**no** (sibling note's C1)")]),
        row(cells: [cell(text: "Live repo-wide consumer"), cell(text: "seed-internal"), cell(text: "cost yes / complexity **no**")]),
      ],
    },
    p(text: "**The gap is real and large. It is migration debt, not a deliberate retirement** — nothing in the tree declares these capabilities unwanted."),

    h2(text: "4. The finding to act on first: `RatchetForever` is very likely mis-declared"),
    p(text: "`lens_contract_complexity` carries `ConstructionJustification { class: RatchetForever }`. That is a **permanence claim**: this class is undecidable, so it can never become a wall and will always be a validating ratchet. DESIGN §5 is explicit that this is the trap to check rather than the safe default:"),
    BlockquoteBlock { blocks: [
      p(text: "*'The word \"never\" is the trap: it lets a ratchet masquerade as a wall, so check decidability before claiming one.'*"),
    ] },
    p(text: "Applied here the claim does not survive contact with its own contents. **Optimality is undecidable by Rice — but most of what is missing is not optimality.** Work and span composition over a closed kernel is decidable. Summation over a *bounded* collection is decidable — that is what the modeled loop bound exists to provide. Output size and peak space over the same bounded fragment are decidable. Interprocedural summaries over an acyclic declaration graph are decidable, and the cyclic case is exactly what SCC plus `DescentEvidence` already decides fail-closed. So `RatchetForever` on the whole contract is a single permanence verdict standing over a **mixed** population, and its effect is to make the anemia unrankable: a class declared permanently undecidable never appears on anyone's list of things to climb."),
    p(text: "**Re-classifying this contract is therefore C0 deliverable (c) (§7)**, splitting the genuinely-undecidable residue (optimality; arbitrary predicate refinement) from the decidable capability that should carry `WallAfterGrounding` with a named trigger. Until that split lands, every phase below is arguing against a declared 'never'."),

    h2(text: "5. The authority ruling (content; signed as C0's first deliverable — §7)"),
    p(text: "Do **not** port `src/v1/complexity.dag` wholesale. It is powerful but coupled to the v1 AST, to parser implementation details, and to string-keyed identity throughout — porting it would cement the seed into the new architecture, which is the one move the project spirit forbids. The split:"),
    CodeBlock { code: "v2.lens.cost              cost + size expressions, work/span composition,\n                          output-size and space expressions, effect demand\n\nv2.lens.complexity        asymptotic projection of cost; dominance and\n                          complexity-class comparison. Nothing else.\n\nstd.realization_schedule  predicted / derived / measured resource accounts\n                          and scheduling consumption\n\nv1.compiler.complexity    legacy realization, capability inventory,\n                          parity oracle, deletion target\n" },
    p(text: "**`SymbolicCost` stays** as the normalized asymptotic projection of the richer `CostExpr` — one authority with two levels of detail, never two competing cost types. The existing `Blocking` cost wall and its bound consumer witness keep working throughout; no phase below may regress them."),

    h2(text: "6. What must NOT be carried across"),
    p(text: "v1's identities are string-keyed in five places, verified: `SizeVar { name: String }`, `SizeLen { collection: String }`, `CostExtern { name: String }`, `CostUnknown { reason: String }`, and `CostInternTable { summaries: Map<String, ComplexitySummary> }`. Every one is the anemic-modeling class DESIGN §2 names — a `String` leaf standing where a grounded identity exists. The migration re-grounds each:"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "function and collection identity → `DeclarationRef` / `ValueIdentity` (the G1 cited-symbol resolution work already makes these resolvable)"),
      li(text: "`CostExtern { name }` → `CostEffect { operation: DeclarationRef }`, joining the sibling note's `ExecuteEffect` atom rather than a second extern channel"),
      li(text: "`CostUnknown { reason: String }` → a typed, located, **countable** cause — a free-text reason cannot be tallied, so its frequency never ranks the deficit for fixing (DESIGN §5)"),
      li(text: "`Certainty = Proven | Conservative` → reconciled with the existing `DescentEvidence` and `Measured` bases rather than minted as a third confidence vocabulary"),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Registry note:** `llvm_instruction_cost` is not merely present in `v2.lens.cost` — it is *registered* as owned by it (`v2.lens.registry` `lens_owned_fn_llvm_instruction_cost`, `owner_module_path: \"v2.lens.cost\"`). Re-homing that uncited machine table to a cited per-target model is therefore a registry change too, not a file move."),

    h2(text: "7. Phases"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**C0 — sign the ruling, census the capabilities, re-classify the boundary.** Exactly three deliverables: **(a)** sign §5's authority ruling — this is the single home for it, and the sibling note depends on it rather than restating it; **(b)** **DELIVERED 2026-08-05** — one typed inventory row per v1 capability, landed as `gunbc.v1_complexity_capability_census` `v1_complexity_capability_roster` with the witness `v1_complexity_capability_census_witness_test`; **(c)** the §4 `RatchetForever` split. **(a)** and **(c)** are operator decisions and remain open. **Accept:** the ruling is signed, no capability is unclassified, and the permanence claim covers only genuinely undecidable rows."),
      li(text: "**C0(b) as landed — what the census carrier owns, and the one arm it added.** The carrier is the authority; this note points at it rather than restating its rows (§6 — no parallel ledger). Two things about its shape are worth stating here because they are decisions, not data. First, **every arm carries required non-empty payloads**, so an unjustified disposition is unwritable rather than lens-caught: `AlreadyInV2` and `AvailableInSharedSubstrate` cannot be claimed without naming the carrier that discharges the capability, `NeedsMigration` without a destination module and owning phase, `SupersededByBetterModel` without what supersedes it. Second, the census **added a sixth arm, `DispositionDeferred`**, carrying an open question and its decider. The five declared arms had no home for a capability whose disposition is one of *this note's own open questions* — parser-progress (question 2) — and forcing it into a neighbouring arm would have fabricated a decision nobody made, inside the artifact whose purpose is to stop guessing at capability status. The arm is deliberately narrow: a row may only defer to a question the design record already asks, and the deferred population is counted so it ranks for closing rather than absorbing. It should be empty at C0 sign-off."),
      li(text: "**C0(b) findings — four things the tree said that this note did not.** Each is executed by the census witness, not asserted in prose. **(1) C4 is materially smaller than §3's table implies.** That table reads 'Call graph / SCC — v1 yes, v2 no', which would make it migration work. It is not: `std.graph` already carries `CallGraph`, forward/reverse adjacency, `dfs_finish_order`, `graph_multi_node_scc_members`, `graph_cycle_members` and `is_valid_proof`; `std.termination` owns `DescentEvidence` and `TerminationProof`; `std.computation` owns `LoweringTarget` and `lower_call_pattern`; `std.induction` owns `CostBound`, `catamorphism_bound` and `derive_bound` — and `v1.compiler.complexity` reaches all of them **by import**, while v2's lens modules import none of them. So the recursion **vocabulary** is already lifted out of the seed and the owed work there is *consumption*, not migration. What is genuinely seed-local is the **derivation layer** — the walkers that produce that vocabulary by traversing the v1 AST, each threading `NewlineIndex` — which is rostered separately. That is the sizing answer the sequencing note says C0 must produce. **(2) `std.induction`'s cost-bound vocabulary belongs on the do-not-re-mint list** and is currently absent from it, so C1 could re-coin a bound taxonomy the substrate already carries. **(3) A migration hazard: `evict_summary` must not carry across.** It does not remove an entry — it overwrites it with `work: CostConst 0, span: CostConst 0, certainty: Proven`, so a later `lookup_summary` on an evicted function reads as *costs nothing, proven* rather than *not computed*. That is the state-space conflation DESIGN names and exactly the zero-for-unmodelled arm the sibling note's honesty states forbid; the capability may migrate, this realization may not. **(4) A receipt for open question 3.** `cost_account_space_from_summary`'s own note says it fills 'CostAccount.space (basis `Derived`)'. It returns a bare `ByteSize?`, constructs no `CostAccount`, and `v1.compiler.complexity` does not import `std.realization_schedule` at all — while `CostBasis` is `Predicted | Measured` with no `Derived` arm anywhere in the tree. The seed already records an intent for a derived basis that the single authority cannot represent, and the function's name is a nickname for what it computes. That makes the three-valued widening a **documented gap with a receipt** rather than a speculative amendment — still the operator's call, but no longer an argument from first principles alone."),
      li(text: "**C1 — one richer expression authority.** Promote `SizeExpr` / `CostExpr` into `v2.lens.cost` with grounded identities per §6; `SymbolicCost` becomes their normalized projection. **Accept:** every existing cost witness stays green (the `Blocking` wall does not regress), and a bounded summation is representable where it currently is not."),
      li(text: "**C2 — `ComplexitySummary` restored.** `work`, `span`, `output_sizes`, `peak_space`, `certainty`, `effect_demand`, with sequential and parallel composition laws matching `std.realization_measurement`'s measured side (sequential: work adds, span adds, space maxes; parallel: work adds, span maxes, space adds). **Accept:** two graphs of equal work and different shape derive different span."),
      li(text: "**C3 — bounded-input evaluation.** *Owned by the sibling note's C1;* listed here only so the dependency is visible. C4 must not begin before it."),
      li(text: "**C4 — interprocedural and recursive analysis.** Declaration-keyed call graph, SCC summaries, summary memoization, descent bounds, worklist/tree/cardinality shapes; parser progress becomes **one specialized consumer** of generic descent facts, not a special case inside the core. Repoint onto `std.termination` / `std.computation` / `v2.std.cardinality` rather than copying v1's walkers. **The largest and highest-risk slice.**"),
      li(text: "**C5 — realization bridge.** Feed the derived summary into `CostAccount`, and split the basis honestly into `Derived | PredictedFromCalibration | Measured` — a closed symbolic derivation and a calibrated machine estimate are different kinds of evidence and today's two-valued basis conflates them. **Accept:** the sibling note's calibration RED (planted omission → falsifier red)."),
      li(text: "**C6 — live consumers, then and only then flip the mode.** Witness-cost admission (the sibling note's C5), floor scheduling demand, and a complexity regression wall catching accidental O(n)→O(n²) over the affected graph. Plus **self-application**: the complexity implementation costs itself or carries a narrow justified exemption. **`AuditOnly` → `Blocking` is the last step, never the first** — an enrolled blocking claim with no live consumer is the inert-lens lie DESIGN §6 forbids."),
      li(text: "**C7 — parity corpus and v1 retirement.** Flat iteration, nested iteration, branch max, output-size growth, recursive tree descent, worklist drain, mutual parser recursion, external effect, unbounded refusal, and the parallel work/span distinction. v2 must preserve every meaningful v1 conclusion while using grounded identities and typed refusals. Then `v1.compiler.complexity` dispositions or deletes."),
    ]),
    p(text: "**Sequencing note:** this runs parallel to the self-host frontier and blocks none of it. It *does* block further expansion of directory-driven `long/` policy, because each new resident deepens the proxy this program exists to retire. Roughly 10–16 merge surfaces. Calendar estimates are deliberately omitted: the C4 slice's size depends on how much of v1's SCC and parser logic is already discharged by landed shared substrate, and that is a C0 output, not a guess to make now. **That output landed 2026-08-05** and it cuts both ways — the SCC and descent *vocabulary* is already shared substrate that v2 need only consume (C0(b) finding 1), while the *walkers* that produce it remain v1-AST-coupled and are the real C4 surface, together with the interprocedural memo. Parser progress is still unsized because its disposition is open question 2."),

    h2(text: "8. Discriminating controls"),
    ul(items: [
      li(text: "A bounded summation derives an exact count where the current engine can only say `ClassLinear`."),
      li(text: "Sequential and parallel graphs of identical work derive **different span** — a span equal to work in both proves span was never derived."),
      li(text: "An interprocedural summary is reused across two call sites (memo hit) and the derived work does not double-count."),
      li(text: "A mutually recursive pair with descent evidence derives a bound; the same pair with descent removed **refuses**, and does not fall back to a class."),
      li(text: "`complexity_variables_admits` rejects at least one input — a validation that admits everything is the current state and must stop being it."),
      li(text: "Every v1 parity-corpus conclusion is reproduced by v2, or is explicitly dispositioned as superseded with a reason."),
      li(text: "The complexity lens applied to itself produces a bound (self-application), or a narrow, named exemption."),
      li(text: "Flipping `lens_contract_complexity` to `Blocking` while `consumer_witness` is still `NoConsumerWitness` **fails** — the mode and the consumer cannot disagree."),
    ]),

    h2(text: "9. Open questions for operator review"),
    ol(items: [
      li(text: "**Is the §4 `RatchetForever` re-classification agreed?** It is the highest-leverage single edit here — while it stands, the anemia is declared permanent and cannot rank for climbing. It is also a *narrowing* of a permanence claim, which is normally a safety-increasing move, but it touches an enrolled contract's boundary class and so deserves an explicit sign-off."),
      li(text: "**Does `parser-progress` survive as a modeled capability, or retire with the seed?** It is v1's most implementation-specific analysis. If the v2 parser reaches its bound through the generic descent facts, this capability is `SupersededByBetterModel` rather than `NeedsMigration` — a C0 answer that materially changes C4's size."),
      li(text: "**Three-valued `CostBasis` (`Derived | PredictedFromCalibration | Measured`) — confirm.** It is a widening of an existing enrolled carrier that the scheduling design signed as two-valued, so it needs an explicit amendment rather than an incidental change."),
      li(text: "**Does the specialized-lens layer collapse?** `complexity_accumulator_copy`, `complexity_lowering`, and `complexity_linearity_audit` are focused rules built around the thin center. Some may dissolve into the richer engine once C2 lands; that would be a §2 win, but each currently has its own contract row and one carries a `WallAfterGrounding` trigger, so the collapse is a decision rather than a cleanup."),
    ]),
  ]
}

data v2_complexity_capability_parity_plan: Plan = Plan {
  slug: "v2-complexity-capability-parity",
  title: "v2 complexity capability parity — restoring the engine, not porting the seed",
  body: v2_complexity_capability_parity_body(),
  dissolution: HasTrigger {
    text: "Delete this doc when the capability census is closed with every v1 row dispositioned, lens_contract_complexity's boundary class distinguishes the genuinely undecidable residue from the decidable capability, v2.lens.cost carries grounded SizeExpr/CostExpr with work/span/output-size/peak-space/certainty on a restored ComplexitySummary, interprocedural summaries and descent bounds derive over declaration-keyed identities, the parity corpus reproduces or dispositions every meaningful v1 conclusion, lens_contract_complexity has a live consumer witness and has flipped off AuditOnly, and v1.compiler.complexity is deleted or dispositioned — at which point the carriers state the capability and this note retires."
  }
}
